          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Physicist and chemist; professor at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-paris">University of Paris</a> from 1906, the first woman to hold such a post there; director of the Curie Laboratory in the Radium Institute, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> (founded 1914); Nobel laureate in Physics (1903) and Chemistry (1911); director of the Red Cross Radiology Service in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></span></div>
